WEBVTT

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:14.200
Thank you all for coming to Flowercrest
Department Store's rooftop planetarium today.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.450
My name is Hoshino Yumemi,
and I am a member of staff at this institution.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.710
Before the projection begins,
I would like to announce a few important things.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.290
Please do not talk—

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.000
I've already heard your opening spiel. Just skip it.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.880
No, that won't do. It is an integral part
of my duties, and thus I cannot omit it.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.850
Right. Do as you please.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.180
Thank you very much.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.770
Please do not talk or whisper during the projection,
as this would be a disturbance to the other customers.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.940
Please turn off your cell phones and any alarms now.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:58.490
In addition, please do not eat, drink,
or smoke at any time during the projection.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.910
And finally, I would like to introduce
a most important partner

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.830
who will take you all into the world of the stars.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.790
Everyone, please welcome her
with a warm round of applause!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.630
I present to you Miss Jena!

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.310
To tell you the truth...

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.890
Miss Jena is...

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.650
the name of this big machine!

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:35.360
Now then, without further ado,
Miss Jena will greet all of you!

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.580
Today, our planetarium was visited

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:54.960
by the 2,487,290th visitor since we first opened.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.180
On behalf of all the staff of our establishment,
I offer you our humblest gratitude.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:06.140
In commemoration of this special occasion,
we have prepared a special projection.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.570
We hope that you will all enjoy it.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.280
On one fine autumn day, it was raining outside.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.500
Rainy days can make you feel a little down.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.960
But please be at ease.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.380
In here, we can summon the Sun whenever we wish.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.800
Here we have our very own Sun.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.340
Slowly, it sets in the western sky.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.430
Ah, here is the first celestial
body to grace our night sky:

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.940
Venus, also known as the Evening Star.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.520
Slowly but surely, the sky is growing darker.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.940
This is our signal to go home.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.910
At last, the curtain of night
slowly falls over the vicinity...

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.330
This is the starry sky at 8:00 pm tonight.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.590
Crossing the ceiling above you
right now is the Milky Way,

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:22.840
so named by civilizations of old who saw it
as a river of milk flowing through the sky.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.850
Now, if you could focus your attention on
the highest star, the one set at the ceiling of the sky.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.520
That is Deneb, the first magnitude
star of the constellation Cygnus.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.650
Close by are Vega of the constellation Lyra,
and Altair of Aquila.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.990
Together, these three make up
what is called the Summer Triangle.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.990
So far, these have all been summer constellations.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.830
Although today has been a very chilly day,

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.950
if you turn your eyes upward
towards the night sky,

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.830
you can still find these final traces of summer.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.960
Now then, shall we turn our attention
to the autumn constellations?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.170
Please look a little east of Deneb.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:08.810
The winged horse is Pegasus,
and the chained princess is Andromeda.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.480
<i>It's like the stars are drawing me in.</i>

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:22.990
Andromeda was the daughter of the ancient
Ethiopian king Cepheus and his queen, Cassiopeia.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.200
Cassiopeia boasted about
her daughter's beauty so greatly,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.200
she invoked the wrath of Poseidon,
god of the ocean.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.250
Angered, Poseidon sent a giant
sea monster to the shores of Ethiopia.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:41.800
Ethiopia was devastated by the
tidal wave caused by the sea monster.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.890
Cepheus received an oracle
saying that to calm Poseidon,

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:51.720
he must sacrifice his daughter Andromeda.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:58.770
Cepheus was torn, but Andromeda
volunteered to sacrifice herself.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:04.900
Reluctantly, Cepheus set aside his sorrows
and chained Andromeda to a rock by the coast.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:11.160
As she lay there trembling,
all alone, the sea rose up.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.790
The sea monster had appeared,

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.790
and it was closing in on Andromeda.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.300
Stuggle as she might, the chains would not yield.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.800
"Save me! Somebody save me!"

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.470
In her mind, Andromeda desperately called for help.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.260
And then, at that very moment!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.350
Riding atop the winged horse Pegasus,
the hero Perseus arrived.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.350
Perseus was on his way back from his
victorious battle against the Gorgon, Medusa.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.110
Noticing that something was amiss
with the shore, he moved closer to check.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.990
<i>Right now, in this very world,
she was an omnipotent storyteller,</i>

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.070
<i>and the stars were her little garden.</i>

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.160
<i>Princesses, heroes, monsters, and gods...</i>

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.370
<i>Each and every one of them
bowed devotedly before her,</i>

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.330
<i>playing their individual parts in the
unfolding drama with absolute obedience.</i>

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.380
And thus did Andromeda and Perseus
become constellations,

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.880
living happily ever after upon
the autumn sky to this day.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.640
Let us now turn to our special projection.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.560
It is named "The Reverie of Mankind
Spreading Its Wings Into Space"...

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.770
What's wrong? Did something break?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.360
<i>Or could it be...</i>

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.580
Here is the fuse board.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:46.090
Mr. Customer, Miss Jena is not responding.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.510
Neither the projectors nor the axes are activating.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.600
What kind of tools will we require
to repair Miss Jena?

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.350
<i>I knew it. The issue wasn't the projector...</i>

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:02.310
It simply won't do for the projection to be
suspended while there are customers viewing it.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.280
We must repair it at once
and restart the projection...

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.190
The power's been cut off.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.410
The power's... been cut off.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.660
My sincerest apologies, but I do not understand.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.660
Somehow or other,

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.000
this facility, by some sort of miracle,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.290
received a weak stream of electrical
power over the past 30 years.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.630
But that's come to an end.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.420
So, you mean there's a power outage?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.930
In that case, the emergency power
will come online soon enough.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:35.970
This place has been supplied by said
emergency power the whole time.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.310
We're out of options.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.560
In that case, when will power be restored?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.100
It won't.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.820
This isn't something someone can fix.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:50.190
In that case, what must we do
in order to restart the projection?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.700
Um, Mr. Customer,

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:58.040
then does this mean that the special projection...

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.750
Listen closely to what I say.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.790
Yes, sir.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:07.630
Continue the projection.
Your voice alone will suffice.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.760
My sincerest apologies, but I do not understand.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.760
I said, continue.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.890
I don't need the projector. I just want to
hear your explanations and commentary.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.140
Can you do that?

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.100
Yes, I certainly can.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:27.190
But if it is just my commentary alone,
then that will not be a projection.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.110
It's okay.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.570
I know all about the stars already.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:36.120
I'll be able to understand everything you
want to show me just from you speaking.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.500
You must be very fond of the stars, Mr. Customer.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.750
I am truly honored to have you
as a customer of our humble establishment.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.210
Yeah.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:56.470
In that case, very well. We will continue
the projection through my explanations alone.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:57.850
This way, please.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.940
<i>She really is trusting.</i>

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.070
I shall now resume the special projection.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:21.580
A very, very, very long time ago...

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.870
Huddled within cold, dark caves,

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.750
the earliest forefathers of humanity lived together.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:35.220
The world was locked in ice, and huge,
tusked beasts still roamed the land.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:40.850
One long, freezing night, a young man woke up.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:45.770
Likely due to a combination of the bitter cold
and gnawing hunger, he was unable to sleep.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:53.480
He rubbed his sleepy eyes, and peered
outside at the entrance of the cave.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.490
Upon the freezing night sky,

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.990
countless numbers of stars twinkled brightly.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.490
Ever since that day,

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:08.620
mankind has never ceased to gaze up
at the heavens in all its vastness with wonder.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:20.800
Was there ever any doubt that humanity would set
its sights beyond the sky, towards space itself?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.600
Towards unknown heights?

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.560
Breaking free of the darkness of night...

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:31.980
Taking the tears of many,
and forging them into the seeds of new dreams...

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.860
And finally, on one fateful day,
those hands grasped outer space.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.240
Here is the third planet of the solar system.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.790
Our planet, Earth.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.040
No matter where on Earth you look,
our planet is teeming with beauty.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:53.250
but currently, there are many disputes, conflicts,

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.050
and problems that can't yet be resolved.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:03.680
Overpopulation, energy, food, space territoriality.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.270
However, it is my sincere belief

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.350
that mankind will be able
to solve all of its problems.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.980
And then, they will reach out
to the heavens above.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:23.990
On this special night,
I would like to let you in on a big secret.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.830
This planetarium is also a time machine!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.340
It allows us to traverse time at will,

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:43.180
from the distant past into
the furthest reaches of the future.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.810
Please take a look.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:54.610
This is the starry sky that will be seen precisely
one thousand years from this day, in this very place.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:12:00.820
Miss Jena the projector, and I, Hoshino Yumemi
the robot, did our best to construct

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.610
this meager starry sky of the future.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:08.990
Please, everyone, don't forget
the starry sky that you saw here.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:16.790
If you ever find yourself lost in the darkness,
no longer able to see the real starry sky,

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:20.010
please remember it.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.260
This is... my little reverie.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.640
Well then, let us return to our own day and age.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.730
The celestial spheres are revolving.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.990
The winter constellations are appearing
above the eastern horizon.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:45.360
Orion, Auriga, Taurus...

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:50.790
These are the harbingers of a magnificent season
that will soon be unfolding every night.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:56.170
The long night has finally ended,
and morning has once again come to the world.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.460
The sun has risen.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.260
The twittering of small birds and
the rustling of the wind are now audible.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.220
The slumbering buildings and trees, too,

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:11.680
are sleepily opening their eyes
to greet the rays of the sun.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:15.230
Very soon, the town will spring to life,

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.650
and just as ever, a new day will begin.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.320
Good morning, everyone.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.660
That marks the end of our special projection.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:31.660
It has been an honor to have you join me,
Hoshino Yumemi, on this journey.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.160
Thank you for listening so attentively.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.470
Mr. Customer, today's projection is over.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.810
Mr. Customer? Mr. Customer?

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.850
It would seem he has fallen asleep.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.690
After taking all the factors into account,

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.320
I think that it would be best to allow
Mr. Customer to sleep like this until morning.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.580
Mr. Customer, Mr. Manager once told me

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:21.540
that it was a great privilege for a human being
to be able to sleep beneath the starry sky.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:27.970
This is why I believe that surely, you must have
enjoyed the special projection, Mr. Customer.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.300
That brings me much joy.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:36.100
<i>I was listening to her as she continued to talk,</i>

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:41.860
<i>and tried to recall how the world
was before the rain began to fall.</i>

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.200
...await you.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.000
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:44.420
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.880
All the stars in the sky await...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.220
Good afternoon, Mr. Customer.
How are you feeling?

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:53.930
Not particularly good, but not too shabby either.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.220
I see.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.180
If you are still feeling ill, by any chance...

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.680
I'm fine.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.850
I see. I am most relieved to hear that.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.440
By the way, Mr. Customer,

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:08.650
my sincerest apologies for
the breakdown during the projection.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.990
I offer you the sincerest apologies
from the bottom of my heart.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:16.240
Well... Your projection wasn't half bad.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.080
I am overjoyed to hear such a compliment.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:24.250
It is also true that you have
helped us out a great deal.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:29.050
Say... Just what do you...

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.550
What is it?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.220
It's nothing.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:37.680
I'm heading off now.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.720
Very well. Thank you for everything.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.100
Offer a prayer for my sake
so that I'll survive the trip back.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.900
To the God of Robots, I mean.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:45.690
Certainly.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.830
Mr. Customer.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:14.170
Excuse me, but may I ask you a question?

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:14.840
What is it?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.390
Will you be in any danger on your journey home?

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:21.470
I could say no, but that would probably be lying.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.690
Will you be taking the train on your way home?

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.770
The trains aren't running.
There's a power outage right now, remember?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:33.240
Then will you be taking a bus or a taxi
or some other kind of vehicle?

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.700
A car, probably.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:41.370
Is your car parked within
a three-kilometer radius of here?

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.540
Sounds about right.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.080
Why are you asking me all this?

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:55.670
I have attempted to contact the support center and
request a release to act upon our professional code,

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.430
but I am unable to connect.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:03.350
As such, I am permitted to act at my own discretion.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:09.520
I will escort you to your car, Mr. Customer.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:10.690
Huh?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:16.820
The duty of escorting the unwell
falls upon us robots.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.200
Are you crazy?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:23.240
No, but I am malfunctioning just slightly.
